==English==

===Etymology===
Past participle of {{m|en|serrate}}, From {{uder|en|la|-}} {{attention|la}} {{m|la|serratus||saw shaped}}, from {{m|la|serra||saw}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Notched or cut like a [[saw]].
#: ''That knife has a '''serrated''' blade.''
# Having a row of [[sharp]] or [[tooth]]-like [[projection]]s.
#: ''Maple leaves have '''serrated''' edges.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|notched}} {{l|en|jagged}}, {{l|en|serrate}}; see also [[Thesaurus:notched]]

